
Data Block:
-----------
      - All the data stored in blocks
      - Smallest unit of Database Storage.
      - A block can have 2KB to 32 KB [8 KB DEFAULT]
      - a BLOCK stores row data or index data
      - block header includes
            - bLOCK TYPE information
            - Table information
            - Row directory
      ==> We can use PCTFREE and PCTUSE parameters to specify the space size in blocks.
            - row overhead
            - number of columns
            - cluster key id
            - ROWID if chained row pieces
            - column length 
            - column value


PGA:
   Memory Area that is dedicated to single user. Every user has its own PGA. Assign ore size of PGA increases performance
- consists below areas.
      1> Session Area
            - Stores session information for each user
            - Stores session variable, login information, session status, etc.
      2> Private SQL Area
            - presistent area
                  - stores the bind variables used in cursor release wen cursor is closed
            - runtime area
                  - execution state
      3>Cursor Area
            - stores information about cursors
      4>SQL Work Area
            - sort area  ==> group by, order by  results
            - Hash Join Area
            - Bitmap merge area
            - Bitmap Create Area

A.] Shared Pool:
    1> Shared SQL Area :
            - Stores execution plan.
            - if same query excuted same execution plan used.
    2> Data dictionary cache:
            - stores metadata of databases
    3> result cache:
            - stores results executed by query 
            - it imporves performance of query which is same used priviously.
    4>Library cache:
            - Container and organizer of shared SQL area.

B] Buffer cache:
            - stores data blocks

